frame "Du Bois 1903, The Souls of Black Folk: double consciousness, looking at oneself through the eyes of others (cited from memory)" reading "a one-way gaze (one side sees, is not seen back as it sees) is a non-symmetric relation; every non-symmetric preorder on 1..4 worlds maps onto the 2-chain (asymmetry.py, checked-finite). That double consciousness is this frame is analogy" -> 3 label checked-finite reach 3 cost 40
frame "Fanon 1952, Peau noire, masques blancs; Bell, critical race theory from the 1970s (interest convergence, 1980); Bonilla-Silva 2003, Racism without Racists (all cited from memory)" reading "ANALOGY (a reading): racism as a structure that persists with no racist intent at any single point; no check here" -> none label open reach 2 cost 40
frame "Anais Nin: exoticizing and racist portrayals of people of colour in her erotica and diaries, as documented by critics (cited from memory, not re-read)" reading "a case of the primitivist move: other peoples cast as closer to nature and the body. A reading of a historical author's texts, not of her person; the documentation is not re-read here" -> none label open reach 2 cost 40
frame "Critique of primitivism: romanticising primitive peoples is a racist move (Torgovnick 1990, Gone Primitive; cited from memory)" reading "ANALOGY (a reading): the noble savage and the savage are one gaze, the 2-chain again; it bears on any anarcho-primitivist lens, see philosophy/ANPRIM.md" -> none label open reach 3 cost 40
record culture/race race checked-finite "culture/race/race.ath: every 2x2 table of nonnegative integers with total N <= 12 (1820 tables): 819 margin classes, 506 with more than one table, the largest has 7 (margins 6 and 6, N = 12); the Frechet bounds max(0, r + c - N) <= a <= min(r, c) are exact in every class. Du Bois's one-way gaze reuses asymmetry.py (non-symmetric preorders map onto the 2-chain). Readings are analogy."
